<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "dashboard.hub">
<!ENTITY author    "LX-S93">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.11.06.2">
<!ENTITY md5       "31e9a0ea06b24542c81d6ae88e1a4097">
<!ENTITY github    "LX-S93/unraid-dashboard">
<!ENTITY gitURL    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/&github;/main">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&gitURL;/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY pkg       "&name;-&version;-x86_64-1">
<!ENTITY cfg       "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" support="https://github.com/&github;/issues" project="https://github.com/&github;" min="7.0.0" icon="tachometer" launch="Dashboard">

<CHANGES>
### 2026.11.06.2
- NVIDIA cards in the Graphics card: load, power against limit, video memory, fan, power state and which containers use the GPU
- New "GPU energy &amp; cost" card: today, this month with forecast, per year, idle draw, 30-day chart, today's power curve and cost per container
- A small collector measures the GPU power every 5 seconds (written to RAM, copied to the flash drive once an hour)
- Electricity price can be changed right in the card
### 2026.11.06.1
- Fix: services and the container fallback could not load Unraid's Docker data
- History charts use the full width right from the start
### 2026.11.06
- First release: a modern overview in the Dashboard tab, Unraid's tile view one click away
- Live processor, memory, graphics, UPS and network cards with short history charts
- Storage at a glance: array, parity check progress, pools and boot device with temperatures and usage
- Containers and VMs: running, needing attention, updates, top CPU and memory users (with Container Hub)
- Services: watches the web interfaces you pick and shows response times
- "Needs attention" strip for disk, temperature, UPS, Tailscale, container and service problems
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
mkdir -p &cfg;
find &cfg; -maxdepth 1 -name '&name;-*.txz' ! -name '&pkg;.txz' -delete
true
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="&cfg;/&pkg;.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>&gitURL;/archive/&pkg;.txz</URL>
<MD5>&md5;</MD5>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
# energy collector for NVIDIA cards (the driver plugin may load after this one at boot)
if [ -f /boot/config/plugins/nvidia-driver.plg ] || [ -x /usr/bin/nvidia-smi ]; then
  echo "* * * * * php /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/include/gpu_collect.php &gt;/dev/null 2&gt;&amp;1" &gt; &cfg;/gpu.cron
else
  rm -f &cfg;/gpu.cron
fi
[ -x /usr/local/sbin/update_cron ] &amp;&amp; /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
true
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " &name; &version; installed"
echo " Open the DASHBOARD tab in the top bar"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
removepkg &pkg; >/dev/null 2>&amp;1
rm -f &cfg;/gpu.cron
[ -x /usr/local/sbin/update_cron ] &amp;&amp; /usr/local/sbin/update_cron
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name; /var/local/&name;
rm -f &cfg;/&name;-*.txz
echo "&name; removed. Settings and the GPU energy log are kept in &cfg;"
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
